ndefined\",\"errorScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{}],\"templateStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"templateScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"notFound\":\"$undefined\",\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]]}],{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"error\":\"$undefined\",\"errorStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"errorScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{}],\"templateStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"templateScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"notFound\":\"$undefined\",\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]]}],{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[\"$L4\",[[\"$\",\"script\",\"script-0\",{\"src\":\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\",\"async\":true,\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]],[\"$\",\"$L5\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$6\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@7\"}]}]]}],{},null,false,null]},null,false,\"$@8\"]},null,false,\"$@8\"]},null,false,\"$@8\"]},null,false,null],[\"$\",\"$1\",\"h\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L9\",null,{\"children\":\"$La\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"hidden\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$6\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.Metadata\",\"children\":\"$Lc\"}]}]}],[\"$\",\"meta\",null,{\"name\":\"next-size-adjust\",\"content\":\"\"}]]}],false]],\"m\":\"$undefined\",\"G\":[\"$d\",[[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/chunks/0-7zhabl4g7ue.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]]],\"S\":true,\"h\":null,\"s\":\"$undefined\",\"l\":\"$undefined\",\"p\":\"$undefined\",\"d\":\"$undefined\",\"b\":\"CCxR80sZRnjlIdOoXSFK7\"}\ne:[]\n8:\"$We\"\nf:I[22016,[\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3shmwh5_nmn.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\"],\"\"]\n10:I[16505,[\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3shmwh5_nmn.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\"],\"LessonClient\"]\n11:T8da,# Managing Teams and Groups\n\nMicrosoft 365 uses groups extensively. The Microsoft Graph PowerShell module lets you manage M365 Groups, Security Groups, and Teams from a single set of cmdlets.\n\n## Understanding Group Types\n\n| Type | Purpose | Has Mailbox | Has Team Site |\n|------|---------|-------------|---------------|\n| **M365 Group** | Collaboration (email, files, calendar) | Yes | Yes |\n| **Security Group** | Access control and licensing | No | No |\n| **Team** | An M365 Group with Microsoft Teams enabled | Yes | Yes |\n\n> **Key Concept:** Every Microsoft Team is backed by an M365 Group, but not every M365 Group has a Team. When you create a Team, a group is created automatically.\n\n## Working with Groups\n\nList and create groups using `Get-MgGroup` and `New-MgGroup`:\n\n```powershell\n# Get all groups\nGet-MgGroup -All\n\n# Filter for a specific group\nGet-MgGroup -Filter \"displayName eq 'Engineering'\"\n\n# Create a new M365 Group\nNew-MgGroup -DisplayName \"Design Team\" -MailEnabled:$true `\n    -MailNickname \"designteam\" -SecurityEnabled:$false `\n    -GroupTypes \"Unified\"\n```\n\nTo create a security group instead, set `-MailEnabled:$false`, `-SecurityEnabled:$true`, and omit `-GroupTypes`.\n\n## Working with Teams\n\nRetrieve Teams information and create channels:\n\n```powershell\n# Get a specific team (requires the group ID)\n$group = Get-MgGroup -Filter \"displayName eq 'Engineering'\"\nGet-MgTeam -TeamId $group.Id\n\n# Create a new channel\nNew-MgTeamChannel -TeamId $group.Id `\n    -DisplayName \"Code Reviews\" -Description \"Channel for code review discussions\"\n```\n\n## Managing Group Members\n\nAdd users to a group using `New-MgGroupMember`:\n\n```powershell\n$group = Get-MgGroup -Filter \"displayName eq 'Design Team'\"\n$user = Get-MgUser -Filter \"userPrincipalName eq 'alex@contoso.com'\"\n\nNew-MgGroupMember -GroupId $group.Id `\n    -DirectoryObjectId $user.Id\n```\n\nTo view current members of a group:\n\n```powershell\nGet-MgGroupMember -GroupId $group.Id | ForEach-Object {\n    Get-MgUser -UserId $_.Id | Select-Object DisplayName, UserPrincipalName\n}\n```\n\n> **Key Concept:** Microsoft Graph cmdlets use object IDs (GUIDs) to reference resources, not display names. You typically look up the ID first with `Get-MgGroup` or `Get-MgUser`, then pass it to other cmdlets.\n4:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-h-screen bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"sticky top-0 z-10 border-b border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/80 backdrop-blur-xl\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-3.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/sharepoint-m365\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-zinc-500 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-300\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M10.5 19.5L3 12m0 0l7.5-7.5M3 12h18\"}]}],\"SharePoint & M365 PowerShell\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/sharepoint-m365/list-items-and-content-types\",\"className\":\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:border-zinc-700 hover:text-zinc-200\",\"title\":\"List Items and Content Types\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M15.75 19.5L8.25 12l7.5-7.5\"}]}]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs tabular-nums text-zinc-500\",\"children\":[5,\" / \",8]}],[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/sharepoint-m365/user-and-license-management\",\"className\":\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:border-zinc-700 hover:text-zinc-200\",\"title\":\"User and License Management\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M8.25 4.5l7.5 7.5-7.5 7.5\"}]}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Managing Teams and Groups\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L10\",null,{\"lesson\":{\"meta\":{\"title\":\"Managing Teams and Groups\",\"description\":\"Administer Teams and M365 Groups.\",\"slug\":\"teams-and-groups\",\"order\":5,\"prerequisites\":[\"m3-l4\"]},\"content\":\"$11\",\"exercises\":[{\"id\":\"m3-l5-ex1\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write the command to get all Microsoft 365 groups using the Microsoft Graph module.\",\"hints\":[\"Use the Get-MgGroup cmdlet.\",\"Add the -All parameter to return all groups.\",\"Try: Get-MgGroup -All\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-MgGroup\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the Get-MgGroup cmdlet.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-All\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Add -All to retrieve all groups (Graph cmdlets page results by default).\"}],\"solution\":\"Get-MgGroup -All\",\"explanation\":\"Get-MgGroup retrieves groups from Microsoft Entra ID via the Graph API. The -All parameter ensures all groups are returned instead of just the first page.\"},{\"id\":\"m3-l5-ex2\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write the command to create a new M365 Group (Unified group) with display name 'Sales Team', mail nickname 'salesteam', mail enabled, and security disabled.\",\"hints\":[\"Use New-MgGroup to create groups.\",\"M365 Groups require -GroupTypes \\\"Unified\\\".\",\"Set -MailEnabled:$true and -SecurityEnabled:$false.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"New-MgGroup\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the New-MgGroup cmdlet.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Sales Team\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Set -DisplayName to 'Sales Team'.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"salesteam\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Set -MailNickname to 'salesteam'.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Unified\",\"hintOnFail\":\"M365 Groups need -GroupTypes \\\"Unified\\\" to distinguish them from security groups.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"-MailEnabled[:\\\\s]+\\\\$true\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Set -MailEnabled:$true for an M365 Group.\"}],\"solution\":\"New-MgGroup -DisplayName \\\"Sales Team\\\" -MailEnabled:$true -MailNickname \\\"salesteam\\\" -SecurityEnabled:$false -GroupTypes \\\"Unified\\\"\",\"explanation\":\"New-MgGroup creates a group in Microsoft Entra ID. The -GroupTypes 'Unified' flag makes it an M365 Group with shared mailbox, calendar, and file storage.\"},{\"id\":\"m3-l5-ex3\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write the command to create a new Teams channel called 'Announcements' with description 'Company-wide announcements' in a team identified by $teamId.\",\"hints\":[\"Use New-MgTeamChannel to create channels.\",\"The -TeamId parameter takes the team's group ID.\",\"Use -DisplayName for the channel name and -Description for the description.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"New-MgTeamChannel\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the New-MgTeamChannel cmdlet.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"-TeamId\\\\s+\\\\$teamId\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pass the team ID with -TeamId $teamId.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"-DisplayName\\\\s+[\\\"']?Announcements[\\\"']?\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Set -DisplayName to 'Announcements'.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"-Description\\\\s+[\\\"']\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Add -Description with the channel description.\"}],\"solution\":\"New-MgTeamChannel -TeamId $teamId -DisplayName \\\"Announcements\\\" -Description \\\"Company-wide announcements\\\"\",\"explanation\":\"New-MgTeamChannel adds a channel to an existing team. You need the team's group ID (a GUID), which you can get from Get-MgGroup.\"},{\"id\":\"m3-l5-ex4\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write the command to filter groups by display name, finding the group named 'Engineering'. Use the -Filter parameter with an OData filter expression.\",\"hints\":[\"Use Get-MgGroup with the -Filter parameter.\",\"OData filter syntax uses: \\\"displayName eq 'value'\\\".\",\"The property name in the filter is displayName (camelCase).\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-MgGroup\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the Get-MgGroup cmdlet.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-Filter\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the -Filter parameter for server-side filtering.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"displayName\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Filter on the displayName property (camelCase).\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Engineering\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Filter for the value 'Engineering'.\"}],\"solution\":\"Get-MgGroup -Filter \\\"displayName eq 'Engineering'\\\"\",\"explanation\":\"The -Filter parameter uses OData query syntax to filter results server-side. This is more efficient than retrieving all groups and filtering with Where-Object.\"}],\"moduleSlug\":\"sharepoint-m365\"}}],\"$L12\"]}]\n12:[\"$\",\"footer\",null,{\"className\":\"border-t border-zinc-800/60\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/sharepoint-m365/list-items-and-content-types\",\"className\":\"group flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-200\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",